description:
**Who we are?**

Ethical Culture Fieldston School is a progressive PreK-12 independent school that has been serving students from throughout New York City and the surrounding suburbs since 1878. ECFS offers a rich curriculum in the arts, sciences, and humanities. A co-ed, nonsectarian school, it serves an inclusive community of about 1,700 students on two campuses - one in the Riverdale section of the Bronx and the other in Manhattan.

**What is essential about working at our school?**

The Ethical Culture Fieldston School has a long history of inclusion and belonging deeply rooted in our mission and the educational philosophy of our founder, Felix Adler. We embrace all aspects of an individual, including their ancestry, family, identity, culture, and beliefs. We affirm both our differences and commonalities and strive to balance individuality and community. In keeping with our progressive tradition, we are dedicated to increasing our students’ cultural literacy to help them understand multiple perspectives and see the world beyond the self.

We expect members of our community to engage in open dialogue about living and learning in an inclusive environment inside and outside the classroom. We see this work, with its creative tensions, as a catalyst for individual and collective growth. On a daily basis, we are committed to making this vision of a democratic, pluralistic, and progressive school a reality.

**Position Summary**

The Director of Financial Aid is the primary point of contact for all families throughout the financial aid process and a visible ambassador for ECFS’s commitment to access and affordability. The Director brings clarity and sound judgment to personal and sensitive conversations, helping every family understand the process.

The Director is responsible for implementing ECFS's financial aid policies, procedures, and practices as well as the management and distribution of financial aid awards in conjunction with the Financial Aid Committee. This position reports to the Chief Strategic Enrollment Officer and serves as a staff resource to the Board of Trustees, the Director manages the aid budget, oversees need assessment and award recommendations across both campuses, and uses data to inform policy, enrollment and long-range financial aid planning.

The hiring range for this position is $115,000-$125,000. When determining the salary for a position, ECFS considers factors including, but not limited to: the scope and responsibilities of the position, internal peer equity, key skills required for the role, the candidate’s work experience, education and training, as well as market and organizational considerations.

*Please note that this is an onsite role and not performed remotely. Ethical Culture Fieldston School retains its right to modify job duties in accordance with changing operational needs.*

**Responsibilities**

Key responsibilities of the Director will include:

* Developing and recommending financial aid strategy that advances the school’s commitment to access and aligns with enrollment goals, including yield, retention and balance across divisions and campuses;
* In partnership with the Chief Strategic Enrollment Officer and the Finance Office, model aid budget, discount rate, and net tuition revenue scenarios, recommending annual financial aid budget and contributing to long-range financial planning;
* Serving as a staff resource to the Board of Trustees and its Finance Committee and, in coordination with the Chief Strategic Enrollment Officer, preparing and presenting financial aid reports and trend analyses to the Board and senior leadership;
* Leading the financial aid review process and assessment for new and continuing families using established standards and guidelines, and recommending award amounts;
* Serving as the primary contact for financial aid applicants and current families;
* Scheduling and leading the Financial Aid Committee meetings, preparing and providing all relevant materials and data;
* Creating and scheduling informational financial aid programming and materials for new and continuing families;
* Managing financial aid systems and vendor relationships, including Clarity;
* Evaluating appeals and recommending appropriate adjustments in award value;
* Partnering with Student Accounts and other departments to align tuition processes and implementing financial aid policy;
* Representing ECFS in ISAAGNY and other related peer networks;
* Building and sustaining trusting relationships with faculty, staff, parents/guardians, students and other constituencies.
* Motivating and inspiring coworkers to achieve goals; and
* Performing other related projects and duties as assigned.

**Position Requirements**

The successful incumbent will possess:

* Five or more years of progressive financial aid experience, preferably in independent schools;
* A Bachelor degree required, Masters degree in related field preferred;
* Excellent time-management and problem solving skills;
* Must possess strong interpersonal and conflict resolution skills with empathy to guide families through difficult financial conversations
* The ability to effectively and diplomatically address the needs of competing constituencies;
* Outstanding oral and written communication skills;
* A high degree of organization, resourcefulness and attention to detail;
* Demonstrated ability to build financial models and analyze data to inform policy and budget decisions;
* Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed;
* Experience working with Clarity, SSS, Finalsite, and Senior Systems is a plus;
* The ability to handle confidential materials with discretion while maintaining a high level of integrity;
* A willingness to learn and embrace new ideas and procedures and a consistent initiative to help streamline processes and improve efficiencies;
* A positive attitude and the ability to listen effectively and be receptive to feed

Langan provides expert Civil, Geotechnical, Traffic and Geo-Environmental engineering consulting services for major developers, renewable energy producers, energy companies, corporations, healthcare systems, colleges/universities, and large infrastructure programs around the world. Our employees collaborate seamlessly and gain valuable hands-on experience that fosters career growth. Langan culture is entrepreneurial from advancing innovative technical solutions, to participating in robust training and knowledge sharing, to making progressive change within the communities we live and work.



Consistently ranked among the top ten "Best Firms to Work For" and Engineering News-Record's top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.

**Job Summary**
---------------

Langan is seeking an experienced **Noise Practice Leader** to drive the growth and advancement of our noise and vibration capabilities. This is a high-impact, seller-doer role responsible for both technical leadership and business development, supporting environmental planning and permitting efforts for land development, transportation, infrastructure, and other complex projects.

This individual will serve as a trusted advisor to clients, a technical authority within Langan, and a practice builder, partnering closely with environmental and firm leadership to expand our presence, strengthen client relationships, and deliver technically sound, defensible environmental solutions. The role will have a primary emphasis on noise and vibration analyses, with opportunities to coordinate across adjacent disciplines such as air quality as needed.

**Job Responsibilities**
------------------------

* Lead the development and expansion of Langan's Noise Practice, including strategy, positioning, and service offerings;
* Identify and pursue new business opportunities, leveraging existing relationships and building new client connections across public and private sectors;
* Drive proposal efforts, scope development, and fee strategy for noise-related services;
* Partner with firm leadership to align noise services with broader environmental, infrastructure, transportation, and land development growth initiatives;
* Serve as a client-facing subject matter expert, advising on noise, vibration, and environmental compliance strategies;
* Build and maintain relationships with developers, agencies, transportation authorities, infrastructure clients, architects, and other key stakeholders;
* Represent Langan in industry forums, client meetings, and regulatory engagement;
* Serve as a lead technical authority for noise and vibration analyses, coordinating with air quality and other multidisciplinary technical teams as appropriate;
* Lead and review noise and vibration technical studies and environmental documentation, ensuring high-quality, technically defensible deliverables;
* Oversee noise modeling, impact assessments, and mitigation strategies across a variety of project types;
* Provide executive-level QA/QC and technical direction across the practice;
* Mentor and grow a high-performing technical team, providing guidance, oversight, and career development support;
* Establish and implement best practices, tools, and methodologies across the noise discipline;
* Serve as an internal thought leader, advising project teams and leadership on complex noise, vibration, and regulatory issues;
* Support project scoping and environmental strategy, including thresholds, methodologies, regulatory requirements, and agency coordination;
* Collaborate with environmental project managers and technical SMEs to integrate noise analyses into broader environmental review and permitting efforts;
* Lead or support responses to agency comments, public review, and technical or regulatory challenges.

**Qualifications**
------------------

* 10+ years of experience leading noise and vibration analyses for environmental, land development, transportation, and/or infrastructure projects;
* Demonstrated success in a seller-doer or practice leadership role, including business development and client relationship management;
* Bachelor's degree in environmental studies, engineering, acoustics, urban planning, or a related field; advanced degree preferred;
* Strong expertise in applicable New York City, New York State, and federal noise and vibration regulatory frameworks, agency guidance, and accepted methodologies;
* Working knowledge of relevant environmental review processes, including NEPA, New York SEQRA, and New York City CEQR, as applicable to noise and vibration studies;
* Strong working knowledge of 23 CFR Part 772 and FHWA noise assessment methodologies for transportation projects;
* Advanced proficiency with FHWA TNM, FHWA RCNM, CadnaA, SoundPLAN, or similar noise modeling tools;
* Experience coordinating noise and vibration analyses with air quality and other environmental disciplines is a plus;
* Experience working with public agencies, transportation authorities, municipalities, developers, and other public- and private-sector clients;
* Proven ability to lead teams, win work, and deliver high-quality technical projects;
* Excellent communication and executive-level client engagement skills.



Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid private medical insurance; group income protection; group life insurance; paid time off including maternity and

**Mavis Tire – Junior Financial Analyst**

**Put your career into high gear with Mavis Tire!**

Mavis is looking for a
**Junior Financial Analyst**
to join our Analytics team at our Operations Support Center in White Plains, New York. With over 4,000 retail locations, Mavis is the largest independently held tire sales and automotive repair chain in the United States. This is a great opportunity for an analytical, detail-oriented professional who enjoys working with data, identifying trends, and turning information into meaningful business insights.

**About the Position**

As a member of the Analytics Department, the Junior Financial Analyst will work closely with the Manager of Analytics and other members of the team to analyze data and develop actionable insights that support business decisions across the organization. The Junior Financial Analyst will compile information from multiple data sources, organize and evaluate findings, and present clear, data-driven recommendations to teams including Executive Leadership, Operations, Finance, Inventory, and Marketing.

**Responsibilities**

The Junior Financial Analyst will:

* Compile and analyze data from multiple sources to identify trends, opportunities, and areas for improvement;
* Develop analyses that provide actionable insights and quantify potential impact on profitability;
* Prepare reports, presentations, and other materials that clearly communicate findings to various audiences;
* Support the Manager of Analytics and other team members with ongoing analytical projects and business initiatives;
* Work with departments across the organization to understand business needs and translate data into meaningful insights; and
* Assist with the continued development of reporting and analytical tools.

**Qualifications**

To be eligible for the position, candidates should possess:

* 1–3 years of experience in financial, business, or marketing analysis;
* Strong Microsoft Excel skills;
* Strong quantitative and analytical abilities;
* Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills;
* Programming experience or a willingness to learn
  **SQL and Power BI/DAX**
  ;
* Strong written communication and presentation skills; and
* Demonstrated ownership and project management skills.

**Employee Benefits**

At Mavis, we understand that our people drive our success. We offer our team members
**competitive weekly pay**
, a positive working environment, and an excellent combination of benefits, including:

* Health, dental, vision, and life insurance;
* 401(k) retirement savings plan with employer match;
* Paid vacation;
* Paid personal and sick time;
* Paid holidays;
* On-the-job training; and
* Opportunities for career growth and advancement.

If you're highly analytical, curious, and ready to grow your career while helping drive data-informed business decisions, we'd love to hear from you.

**Apply today and put your career into high gear with Mavis!**

***Mavis is an Equal Opportunity Employer***

Columbia Bank is a full-service consumer and commercial bank serving individuals, businesses, and communities across New Jersey, Staten Island, and Brooklyn. Through our banking, title, insurance, and wealth management businesses, we provide a broad range of financial solutions tailored to our customers’ needs. We are also committed to strengthening the communities we serve through employee volunteerism, community partnerships, and the Columbia Bank Foundation.

**Why this role Matters****:** As a Full Time Universal Banker you will provide a full range of banking services to retail customers; including both transactional and non-transactional processes. Offers customers more personal banking options while still providing traditional services and assists in reaching all goals set for the branch.

**What You'll Deliver/Areas of Impact****:**

* Processes all banking transactions including but not limited to; deposits, withdrawals, transfers, cashing checks, money orders, selling money orders, gift and Bank checks, processing loan payments and safe deposit box rentals. All banking transactions are to be processed through Columbia Bank’s on-line terminals;
* Opens new deposit and checking accounts of all kind and explains these products to customers as required. Handles deceased accounts. Assists with maintenance of files and any documentation of daily platform work required. Assists customers with safe deposit boxes, answers inquiries or provides explanations of all products and services including renegotiation of CDs;
* Discusses personal financial needs with customers and makes recommendations on how the Bank can meet those needs. Cross sells Bank’s products and services. Interacts with other Bank departments as required. Services customers, in person or via the telephone, to answer inquiries, research and resolve customer problems and/or complaints and ensure customer satisfaction. Explains the features and benefits of on-line banking and how it works;
* Prepares daily proof sheet at close of business each day. Helps with end of day closing procedures for the branch which includes, but is not limited to; preparation of branch consolidation sheet and document imaging of required branch work;
* Maintains accurate customer and account records. Maintains and updates safe deposit box records, back office work and ordering checks and maintaining branch files;
* Makes referrals to the Wealth Management area of the Bank, First Jersey Title, Mortgage Origination and other departments of the Bank as appropriate;
* Performs other job related duties as assigned.

**What You'll Need to Succeed:**

* High school diploma required or a Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Business, or Finance is preferred;
* 1-2 years of retail or customer service experience required;
* Knowledge of financial products preferred;
* Interpersonal, time management, organizational and PC skills a must;
* Excellent verbal and written communication skills required;
* Ability to work weekends as needed or scheduled;
* Ability to lift up to 20 lbs.;
* Candidates must attend mandatory training, continued employment is contingent upon passing training classes.

**Technology Qualifications****:**

* Independent and highly motivated self-starter;
* Results oriented with proven track record to motivate self and others to accomplish objectives;
* Dedicated, enthusiastic, and driven; possesses a strong work ethic;
* A collaborator and team player, translating knowledge and experience into strong and productive relationships;
* Ability to deliver a seamless experience to the customer.

**Orientation, Onboarding & Training:**

We provide you the training to help you excel in your position. In order to maximize on your experience we have a robust Onboarding & Orientation Process. Universal Banker positions require either part-time or full-time training for 10 business days. Training schedules are based on availability.

**How We Take Care of You:**

Build a stronger future for yourself, your family and the communities we serve. At Columbia Bank, meaningful work comes together with a collaborative and rewarding culture, opportunities to learn and grow, and a total rewards package designed to support your health, financial security and overall wellbeing. Benefits include healthcare choice, retirement savings with company support, employee ownership, wellness resources, education and student loan programs, paid time off and financial protection. Join a company where your contribution is valued, your growth is supported and your career can make a meaningful impact.

* + Medical, Dental, Vision and Rx which are contributory.
  + Bonus programs.
  + Employee Stock Option Program (ESOP).
  + Life Insurance, Long Term Disability and Accidental Death and Dismemberment (LTD&AD&D).
  + Paid Time Off (PTO) which includes Personal and Vacation Time.
  + Paid Sick Time.
  + Bank Holidays.
  + Employees may participate in the 401k program.

**The hours that you will dedicate to work****:**

Monday to Friday: 8:30am until closing, working 40 hours, must be able to work alternating Saturdays: 8:30am until closing based on business needs.

Columbia Bank and its affiliates is an Equal Opportunity Employer, including individuals with disabilities and veterans.

