**Director**
============

* ADMIN FOR CHILDREN'S SVCS

Posted on

11/04/2026

* Full-time

Location

MANHATTAN

* Exam may be required

Department

Office of Referral Mgmt (DPS)

Salary range: $98,140.00 – $131,956.00

Save

**Job Description**
-------------------

THE SELECTED CANDIDATE WILL BE OFFERED A SALARY BETWEEN $98,140.00 - $112,883.00


THIS POSITION IS ONLY OPEN TO CANDIDATES WHO ARE PERMANENT (NOT PROVISIONAL) IN THE CIVIL SERVICE TITLE OF ADMINISTRATIVE STAFF ANALYST.


The Administration for Children’s Services (ACS) protects and promotes the safety and well-being of children and families through child welfare and juvenile justice services and community supports. ACS manages community-based supports and foster care services, and provides subsidized child care vouchers. ACS child protection staff respond to allegations of child maltreatment. In juvenile justice, ACS oversees detention, placement and programs for youth in the community.


The Family Services Division (FSD) and its network of contracted providers deliver one of the largest and most diverse continuums of community-based child welfare prevention services in the nation, improving safety, well-being, and permanency for thousands of families and children each year. FSD focuses on systems improvement, innovation, and strategic initiatives that require collaboration with major community partners to address urgent or emerging provider and family needs, city or state mandates, and high-priority strategic goals of ACS leadership.


The Office of Program Management & Sustainability (OPMS) oversees a dynamic portfolio of multi-partner projects that advance prevention strategies, foster innovation, and ensure the sustainability of evidence-based programs within the child welfare system. This role manages cross-functional teams spanning program development, systems, data analysis, and practice support. This position is critical to overall operations, supporting our contracted preventive agencies and other key partners to improve safety, well-being, and permanency outcomes for children and families, and to enhance provider agencies' capacity to deliver comprehensive services and meet performance goals.


The Program Design and Implementation (PDI) team within the Office of Program Management and Sustainability develops and implements strategies to ensure that the full continuum of prevention programs is implemented in alignment with service model fidelity and in full compliance with NYC child welfare requirements. The PDI team provides ongoing contract management and support to help providers meet contract expectations the PDI Team is seeking an outstanding candidate to serve as the Director of School-Based Early Support Programs.


School-Based Early Support is a new program type that reflects ACS’ goal to partner closely with schools to connect families to supports and services well before concerns warrant a child welfare investigation. SBES programs offer families a menu of flexible service options that connect them to community resources through case management, address concrete needs, support parents/caregivers, and prevent further involvement in the child welfare system.


The Director of School-Based Early Support programs will report to the Executive Director or Assistant Commissioner of Program Design and Implementation (PDI) to carry out various duties, including but not limited to:


* Manage the day-to-day operations of the School-Based Early Support (SBES) team and the portfolio of programs;
* Develop and streamline processes for program monitoring, ongoing implementation, budget, and invoice review;
* Oversee the strategy for cohorts among SBES contracted providers to strengthen the practice, address challenges, and share lessons learned;
* Collaborate with external partners from the NYC Department of Education as needed to support effective program implementation and ongoing service delivery;
* Lead the development and continuous improvement of the unit’s strategy to define and impact metrics for individual programs and across the cohort of School-Based Early Support programs;
* Propose strategies, develop guidance and inform policy and planning for the School-Based Early Support programs and partner with internal divisions and contracted providers to continuously improve delivery of services, including by promoting racial equity and social and economic justice, and by ensuring families have a voice in the services they receive;
* Build a strong understanding of contract and program expectations, ACS standards for prevention service delivery, and strengthen case practice to families and overall system performance in collaboration with other FSD units and ACS’ Division of Policy, Planning, and Measurement (DPPM);
* Implement the use of qualitative and quantitative methods to understand better SBES program operations and performance, including utilization and family engagement, and to drive programmatic improvement and evaluation;
* Prepare summary reports on fiscal and programmatic concerns and directly monitor the SBES program performance and their alignment to contract requirements;
* Provide support to SBES providers in their program development of more efficient/effective approaches to program administration;
* Provide technical assistance to SBES providers to support reporting processes;
* Review and finalize documents, presentations, and facilitate goal-oriented meetings with key partners to generate buy-in, improve the quality of families’ experiences and circumstances, and effectively manage projects and workstreams;
* Ensure that the team conducts site and field visits, engages community members to inform program planning, and builds relationships with providers, developers, front-line staff, and internal/external partners;
* Supervise staff and interns on tasks and projects, as needed.



ADDITIONAL

**Summary**

Founded in Florence, Italy, in 1921, Gucci is one of the world’s leading luxury brands. Under the leadership of President and CEO Francesca Bellettini and the artistic direction of Demna, the House continues to redefine luxury and fashion while celebrating creativity, Italian craftsmanship, and innovation.

Gucci is part of the global luxury group Kering, which manages renowned Houses in fashion, leather goods, jewelry, and eyewear.

**Job Description**



**Role Mission**



The Client Services team is an internal hub that collaborates cross-functionally with corporate departments and stores to ensure a 360-degree omni-channel client experience.



As the Gucci Client Services Team Manager, will assist the Senior Manager in leading and directing all activities required to achieve Client Services objectives. In this role, you will be responsible for overseeing all client inquiries, case management processes/fulfillment, and client resolution, reporting, and the development of best practices to contribute to the efficiency of the department. This position will represent the brand as a Gucci Ambassador by promoting the values and ambitions within the luxury marketplace.



**Key Accountabilities**



* Oversee the day-to-day operations of the assigned department to ensure that department goals, such as service level, quality, and staffing, are met;
* Develop strong relationships with clients to ensure maximum satisfaction and increase client loyalty and retention;
* Clear understanding of all company Key Performance Indicators (KPI), monitor weekly reporting for utilization in daily and monthly performance coaching conversations;
* Accountable for analyzing and prioritizing daily incoming work and managing back-up processing support accordingly;
* Identify orders requiring special needs and handling in partnership with the operations team;
* Evaluate, identify, and support opportunities to drive process improvements that will increase accurate output from clients and stores;
* Prepare and direct scheduling, monitor attendance, punctuality, vacation time-off planning, shift schedules, breaks/lunches, training, and offline activities;
* Review eCommerce sales daily and assess high value / exceptional orders requiring follow up, potentially adding to the Very Important Gucci Clients (VIG) list;
* Monitor calls to observe desired demeanor, accuracy, consistency to ensure that company policies and procedures and service levels are being adhered to;
* Conduct monthly coaching/counseling sessions with employees to review performance and provide timely feedback;
* Train and develop direct reports for future growth and career development;
* Control workflow through the understanding and enforcement of all company policies and procedures;
* Ensure team compliance to all company HR and operational policies and procedures;
* Compile and generate reports as they relate to customer service;
* Monitor website to bring customer-related improvements and issues to the eCommerce and merchandising team;
* Point of contact for client advisor in case of website issues;
* Ability to work both collaboratively as part of a team as well as independently.


**Key Requirements**



* Experience with call center phone management and contact volume reporting a plus;
* Knowledge of Salesforce, Oracle, Cybersource and stock inventory systems preferred;
* Proven ability to manage complex and competing priorities;
* Intermediate to advance computer skills;
* Able to work in fast-paced environment, managing multiple channels at the time;
* Confident to resolve customer complaints and manage escalated inquiries effectively;
* Excellent interpersonal written, phone and communication skills;
* Ability to develop and manage performance;
* A focus on quality and extensive passion for and knowledge of Gucci products;
* An excellent, collaborative approach to teamwork and flexible working style;
* Proficiency in multiple languages highly desirable;
* Must be available to work a flexible work schedule which will include evenings, weekends, and holidays;
* Demonstrates a high level of energy and enthusiasm.


**Work Authorization**



* Qualified candidates must have the proper work authorization to work in the United States


